<Project Sdk="Microsoft.NET.Sdk">
  <PropertyGroup>
    <SharedKernelTier>Abstractions</SharedKernelTier>
    <!-- NuGet packaging metadata -->
    <Description>The CQRS vocabulary a .NET service's Application project speaks, owned by the kernel rather than by a mediator library: requests, commands, queries and their handlers, the sender, the pipeline-behavior contract, domain-event handlers, and the markers that opt a request into authorization, validation, idempotency, auditing, logging and caching.

Every handler returns Result or Result&lt;T&gt;, so an expected failure is a value the caller must handle rather than an exception thrown past it. ICommandBase and IQueryBase let a pipeline behavior constrain to "any command" or "any query" once, so behaviors that must not touch reads are never resolved for them.

This package declares shapes and performs no I/O, and it references no mediator: MediatR is used only by SharedKernel.Application.Mediator.MediatR, so replacing it changes no command, query, handler or behavior. The behaviors themselves live in SharedKernel.Application.Pipeline. Depends only on SharedKernel.Primitives, SharedKernel.Domain and SharedKernel.Caching.Abstractions.</Description>
    <PackageReleaseNotes>First release.

WHAT IS IN IT
- Requests: IRequest&lt;TResponse&gt;, IRequestHandler&lt;,&gt;, ISender (Send, CreateStream) and IPipelineBehavior&lt;,&gt; with RequestHandlerContinuation&lt;TResponse&gt;.
- Commands and queries: ICommandBase, ICommand, ICommand&lt;TResponse&gt;, IQueryBase, IQuery&lt;TResponse&gt;, and the handler aliases ICommandHandler&lt;&gt;/ICommandHandler&lt;,&gt;/IQueryHandler&lt;,&gt;.
- Streaming reads: IStreamQuery&lt;TResponse&gt;, IStreamQueryHandler&lt;,&gt; and IStreamPipelineBehavior&lt;,&gt;.
- Domain events: IDomainEventHandler&lt;TDomainEvent&gt;.
- Pipeline markers and ports: IAuthorizeRequest/PermissionMatch, IIdempotentRequest, IAuditableRequest&lt;TResponse&gt;, ILoggableRequest&lt;TResponse&gt;, ICacheableQuery&lt;TValue&gt;, IInvalidatesCache, CacheScope, CacheKeyRef, ICommandScope and IRequestValidator&lt;TRequest&gt;.

THINGS WORTH KNOWING BEFORE YOU ADOPT IT
- A request's response must be Result or Result&lt;T&gt; when it uses a pipeline marker. Several pipeline behaviors short-circuit by constructing a failed response, which no other response type can express; SharedKernel.Analyzers' SK0040 flags the mistake at build time.
- Streams run only IStreamPipelineBehavior registrations, never request behaviors, and stream items are deliberately not wrapped in Result&lt;T&gt;.
- Domain events dispatch serially through DomainEventDispatcher (SharedKernel.Application.Pipeline), before the physical save.

See the package README for the decision guide, the walkthrough and the full reference.</PackageReleaseNotes>
    <PackageTags>cqrs;mediator;application;command;query;streaming;domain-events;shared-kernel</PackageTags>
    <GenerateDocumentationFile>true</GenerateDocumentationFile>
    <WarningsAsErrors>$(WarningsAsErrors);nullable;CS1591;RS0016;RS0017;RS0022;RS0024;RS0025;RS0036;RS0037</WarningsAsErrors>
  </PropertyGroup>
  <ItemGroup>
    <!--
      Abstractions tier: no mediator library and no implementation. CachePolicy (ICacheableQuery) is
      the only reason for the SharedKernel.Caching.Abstractions reference, which is itself
      dependency-free.
    -->
    <ProjectReference Include="..\..\01.Core\SharedKernel.Primitives\SharedKernel.Primitives.csproj" />
    <ProjectReference Include="..\..\03.Domain\SharedKernel.Domain\SharedKernel.Domain.csproj" />
    <ProjectReference Include="..\..\02.Caching\SharedKernel.Caching.Abstractions\SharedKernel.Caching.Abstractions.csproj" />
  </ItemGroup>
  <ItemGroup>
    <PackageReference Include="Microsoft.CodeAnalysis.PublicApiAnalyzers" PrivateAssets="all" />
    <AdditionalFiles Include="PublicAPI.Shipped.txt" />
    <AdditionalFiles Include="PublicAPI.Unshipped.txt" />
  </ItemGroup>
</Project>
